{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-gauge-action-groupoid","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:gauge-action-groupoid","kind":"definition","title":"Gauge action groupoid","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-action","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-lagrangian"],"tags":["appendix","standard-model","gauge-theory","groupoid","action"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.StandardModel.GaugeActionGroupoid","text":"gauge-action-groupoid.md","leanSource":"gauge-action-groupoid.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:gauge-action-groupoid\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code> be an additive abelian group of action values. A <strong>gauge action groupoid</strong> over <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code> is a groupoid <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{G}</code> — objects the <em>topological states</em> (knot and braid configurations), morphisms the <em>gauge transformations</em> (reversible deformations, braiding operations, cobordism moves) — equipped with an action functional</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathrm{act} \\colon \\mathrm{Hom}_{\\mathbf{G}}(X, Y) \\to R</code></pre>\n<p>satisfying, for all states <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X, Y, Z</code> and composable gauge transformations <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f \\colon X \\to Y</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">g \\colon Y \\to Z</code>,</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathrm{act}(\\mathrm{id}_X) = 0,\n  \\qquad\n  \\mathrm{act}(g \\circ f) = \\mathrm{act}(f) + \\mathrm{act}(g).</code></pre>\n<p>Two states <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X, Y</code> are <strong>gauge equivalent</strong> when <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Hom}_{\\mathbf{G}}(X, Y) \\neq \\emptyset</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-standard-model/gauge-action-groupoid.md","heading":"Definition","number":"27.1.1","page":"b/def-gauge-action-groupoid","qa":{"counts":{"pass":54,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":10,"unknown":0,"stale":63}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.StandardModel.GaugeActionGroupoid","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-standard-model/gauge-action-groupoid.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
